 steps to take, and how to validate everything with a reference backtest.\\n\\nLooking at the codebase, I can see the multi-agent pipeline is already in place with the graph setup, shared state management, and backtest engine integration. The unit tests cover signal parsing and graph invocation well, but there's a documentation gap — the strategy exists and works but isn't documented as a first-class reference, there's no minimal config profile for running an end-to-end backtest, and the integration testing could be more comprehensive.\\n\\nI'm also noticing a potential schema mismatch: the `LLMAgentStrategy` expects `reasoning` and `decision_report` fields from the graph output, but these aren't defined in the `IndicatorAgentState` TypedDict, which suggests the decision agent is outputting extra fields that fall outside the state schema. I need to verify whether the `reasoning` field is consistently populated from the graph and properly mapped to the signal's `analysis_summary`.\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":474,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":59803,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":474},\"output_tokens\":8,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"ce2496a8-a497-4f7a-9d36-07ca768dd87e\",\"uuid\":\"3e3fea3c-1bcd-4c06-988e-e9f1f2246e50\"}\ndocs/envelopes/QuantAgent-c69/20260505T005214Z-QuantAgent-c69-planner/executor-stdout-claude-code.log:4968:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-6\",\"id\":\"msg_01WLZiDcM7EsiJZDsdhnD756\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_015dXP4iLRdFFxx6iFCVvcEi\",\"name\":\"Write\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/tmp/autodev-worktrees/QuantAgent/QuantAgent-c69/planner-20260505T005036