. Here's the structured output:\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Result: SUCCESS\\n\\n**Run ID**: `20260505T005214Z-QuantAgent-c69-planner`\\n\\n### Key Finding\\n\\n`LLMAgentStrategy.generate_signal()` has a critical gap: the decision agent returns a `TradingDecision` Pydantic object, but the strategy reads `result.get(\\\"reasoning\\\", \\\"\\\")` — a key that doesn't exist in graph state. Reasoning is actually at `result[\\\"final_trade_decision\\\"].reasoning`. As a result, every signal is persisted with `analysis_summary = \\\"LLM Agent analysis\\\"` (static fallback), never with real agent reasoning.\\n\\nThe fix is 2 lines in `generate_signal()`. Existing tests don't catch this because they mock the graph returning plain strings, not `TradingDecision` objects.\\n\\n### Artifacts Produced\\n\\n| File | Type |\\n|------|------|\\n| `docs/02_planning/QuantAgent-c69-PL-llm-agent-strategy-m1.md` | Planning — step-by-step implementation plan |\\n| `docs/05_acceptance_tests/QuantAgent-c69-AC-llm-agent-strategy.md` | AC — 6 testable Given/When/Then criteria |\\n| `docs/06_implementation/QuantAgent-c69-IM-llm-agent-strategy.md` | IM — code snippets, test templates, reference backtest profile |\\n| Updated 3 README index files | Index |\\n| Envelope artifacts (result.json, run-report.md, quality-gates.log, commands.log) | Envelope |\\n\\n### Files the Implementer Must Touch\\n\\n- `quantagent/strategy/llm_agent_strategy.py` — fix `generate_signal()` to extract from `TradingDecision` Pydantic object\\n- `tests/test_llm_agent_strategy.py` — add `TestTradingDecisionObjectPath` class (snippets in IM doc)\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":939,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":81242,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":939},\"output_tokens\":1,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":nul