q/.../result.json` | Machine-readable result |\\n| `docs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/.../run-report.md` | Human-readable summary |\\n| Beads comment on `QuantAgent-uzq` | Added ✓ |\\n\\n### Next step\\n\\n**implementer phase** — apply changes to exactly 2 files:\\n1. `quantagent/trading/scheduler.py` — add `SchedulerHeartbeat` import + 2 new methods + 2 calls in `analyze_and_trade()`\\n2. `tests/trading/test_scheduler.py` — replace `DummySession.query()` body with self-referential mock\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"2b9b65c5-e77e-400b-90aa-d1fae3699661\",\"total_cost_usd\":0.9627328,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":18,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":80622,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":968261,\"output_tokens\":24419,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":80622,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":605,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":78248,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2374,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":2374},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":3483,\"outputTokens\":20,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.003583,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":18,\"outputTokens\":24419,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":968261,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":80622,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.9591498,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"356624d7-4932-4071-b1b4-9173f1dc4c73\"}\ndocs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T074433Z-QuantAgent-uzq-integration/integration-decision-20260509T074433Z.md:19:- Planner artifact: `docs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T023809Z-QuantAgent-uzq-planner/result.json`\ndocs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T074433Z-QuantAgent-uzq-integration/integration-decision-20260509T074433Z.md:20:- Implementer artifact: `docs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/result.json`\ndocs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T074433Z-QuantAgent-uzq-integration/integration-decision-20260509T074433Z.md:21:- Tester artifact: `docs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T074327Z-QuantAgent-uzq-tester/result.json`\ndocs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/router-result.json:50:    \"result.json\",\ndocs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/router-result.json:51:    \"run-report.md\",\ndocs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/router-result.json:54:  \"executor_result_json_source\": \"/home/azureuser/repos/projects/QuantAgent/docs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/result.json\",\ndocs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/input-envelope.md:136:- Cambiar `.github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml`\ndocs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/router-output-claude-code.md:53:- Result JSON: `/home/azureuser/repos/projects/QuantAgent/docs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/result.json`\ndocs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/route-plan-claude-code.json:20:    \"run_report\": \"/home/azureuser/repos/projects/QuantAgent/docs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/run-report.md\",\ndocs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/route-plan-claude-code.json:21:    \"result_json\": \"/home/azureuser/repos/projects/QuantAgent/docs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/result.json\",\ndocs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/executor-prompt-claude-code.md:10:        - Write canonical artifacts under the declared artifacts dir whenever possible: `result.json`, `run-report.md`, `commands.log`, `quality-gates.log`.\ndocs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/executor-prompt-claude-code.md:207:- Cambiar `.github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml`\ndocs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/issue.json:4:  \"description\": \"## Contexto\\nLa revalidación de `QuantAgent-82t` sobre `main` con PostgreSQL local mostró 8 fallas pre-existentes concentradas en los tests del scheduler/heartbeat.\\n\\n## Comando verificado\\n`DATABASE_URL=postgresql://test:***@localhost:5432/quantagent_test /mnt/actions-runner/autodev-runtime/venvs/QuantAgent/.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/test_vje_scheduler_heartbeat_backend.py tests/trading/test_scheduler.py -v --tb=short --maxfail=10 -m \\\"not integration and not slow\\\"`\\n\\n## Fallas verificables\\n### Heartbeat backend (`tests/test_vje_scheduler_heartbeat_backend.py`)\\n- `test_upsert_heartbeat_start_updates_existing_row_for_environment`\\n- `test_upsert_heartbeat_complete_sets_last_trade_id`\\n- `test_analyze_and_trade_continues_when_heartbeat_start_fails`\\n- `test_analyze_and_trade_full_cycle_writes_completed_heartbeat`\\n- `test_analyze_and_trade_per_asset_error_completes_heartbeat_with_error_count`\\n\\nSíntomas observados:\\n- `TradingScheduler` ya no expone `_upsert_heartbeat_start`\\n- `analyze_and_trade()` no llama al mock `_upsert_heartbeat_complete`\\n- no se persiste ninguna fila `SchedulerHeartbeat` en el ciclo real\\n\\n### Scheduler unit tests (`tests/trading/test_scheduler.py`)\\n- `test_trading_scheduler_long_signal_executes_order`\\n- `test_trading_scheduler_short_signal_executes_order`\\n- `test_trading_scheduler_hold_signal_skips_execution`\\n\\nSíntoma observado:\\n- `stats[\\\"processed\\\"] == 0` porque `DummySession.query()` devuelve un `Mock`, el scheduler lo interpreta como posición activa y `PositionMonitor.update_candle_tracking()` rompe con `TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for +=: 'Mock' and 'int'`\\n\\n## Cambio requerido\\nAlinear implementación y/o tests del `TradingScheduler` con el contrato actual después de la integración de PositionMonitor y del feature de scheduler heartbeat, para que estos tests vuelvan a pasar de forma reproducible en `main`.\\n\\n## Criterio de aceptación\\n- [ ] Los 5 tests fallidos de `tests/test_vje_scheduler_heartbeat_backend.py` pasan\\n- [ ] Los 3 tests fallidos de `tests/trading/test_scheduler.py` pasan\\n- [ ] El comando exacto del gate de `QuantAgent-82t` deja de frenarse por estos módulos\\n\\n## Archivos relevantes\\n- `quantagent/trading/scheduler.py`\\n- `quantagent/trading/position_monitor.py`\\n- `tests/test_vje_scheduler_heartbeat_backend.py`\\n- `tests/trading/test_scheduler.py`\\n- `quantagent/models.py`\\n\\n## Fuera de scope\\n- Cambiar `.github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml`\\n- Corregir `tests/test_wait_sec_deprecation_removal.py`\\n\",\ndocs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/issue.json:15:      \"title\": \"Re-enable unit tests in CI pipeline (main-ci-deploy.yml)\",\ndocs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/issue.json:16:      \"description\": \"El step de pytest en `.github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml` está comentado (\\\"Unit tests temporarily disabled\\\"). El CI actual solo corre lint, permitiendo que código roto llegue a QA. Con QuantAgent-sfc y QuantAgent-4ch resueltos, la suite estará limpia.\\n\\nEl workflow ya tiene un servicio PostgreSQL efímero configurado (postgres:16, DB `quantagent_test`, puerto 5432).\\n\\n**Cambio requerido:**\\n1. Descomentar el step \\\"Run unit tests\\\" en `main-ci-deploy.yml`\\n2. Comando: `pytest tests/ -v --tb=short --maxfail=10 -m \\\"not integration and not slow\\\"`\\n3. Sin `continue-on-error: true` — debe bloquear el deploy si hay fallos\\n4. Verificar que `DATABASE_URL` esté disponible en el env del step\\n\\n**Criterio de aceptación:**\\n- Step \\\"Run unit tests\\\" habilitado y corriendo en cada push a main\\n- Push con tests fallando bloquea el deploy a QA y notifica Telegram\\n- Push con tests pasando despliega a QA normalmente\\n\\n**Archivos relevantes:**\\n- `.github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml` — step comentado ~líneas 47-55\\n- `pytest.ini` — markers: slow, integration, api, vision\\n\\n**Fuera de scope:** no modificar los tests, no tocar main-ci.yml (ticket separado QuantAgent-ng1).\\n\\n**Bloqueado por:** QuantAgent-sfc, QuantAgent-4ch\\n\",\ndocs/06_implementation/QuantAgent-uzq-IM-fix-scheduler-heartbeat.md:228:- `.github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml` — out of scope\ndocs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/router-run-report.md:53:- Result JSON: `/home/azureuser/repos/projects/QuantAgent/docs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/result.json`\ndocs/06_implementation/README.md:36:- [QuantAgent-app-IM-qa-streamlit-cutover.md](./QuantAgent-app-IM-qa-streamlit-cutover.md) - QA Streamlit cutover, Cloudflare tunnel alignment, and deploy_finished -> qa_verified contract.\ndocs/06_implementation/QuantAgent-app-IM-qa-deploy-notify-metadata.md:13:- Added `actions/checkout@v4` as the first step in `jobs.deploy-qa.steps` of `.github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml`.\ndocs/06_implementation/QuantAgent-app-IM-qa-deploy-notify-metadata.md:31:- Parsed `.github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml` with Python/YAML and asserted:\ndocs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/executor-stdout-claude-code.log:32:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01NHUEXpeNgrkPmTcAsXRWH7\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t# QuantAgent-uzq — Implementation: Fix TradingScheduler Heartbeat and Scheduler Unit-Test Regressions\\n2\\t\\n3\\t**Issue ID:** QuantAgent-uzq  \\n4\\t**Phase:** implementer  \\n5\\t**Acceptance tests:** `docs/05_acceptance_tests/QuantAgent-uzq-AC-fix-scheduler-heartbeat.md`\\n6\\t\\n7\\t---\\n8\\t\\n9\\t## Root Cause Analysis\\n10\\t\\n11\\t### Problem 1 — Missing heartbeat methods in `TradingScheduler`\\n12\\t\\n13\\tThe `SchedulerHeartbeat` model (`quantagent/models.py:375`) and its tests (`tests/test_vje_scheduler_heartbeat_backend.py`) were written expecting two private methods on `TradingScheduler`:\\n14\\t\\n15\\t- `_upsert_heartbeat_start(started_at: datetime) -> Optional[SchedulerHeartbeat]`\\n16\\t- `_upsert_heartbeat_complete(heartbeat: Optional[SchedulerHeartbeat], stats: dict) -> None`\\n17\\t\\n18\\tThese methods were never added to `quantagent/trading/scheduler.py`. The `analyze_and_trade()` method (line 148) also never calls them.\\n19\\t\\n20\\t### Problem 2 — `DummySession.query()` returns an incomplete mock chain\\n21\\t\\n22\\t`PositionMonitor.get_active_position()` (`quantagent/trading/position_monitor.py:26-36`) chains:\\n23\\t```python\\n24\\tself.db.query(ActivePosition).filter(...).filter(...).order_by(ActivePosition.id).first()\\n25\\t```\\n26\\t\\n27\\t`DummySession.query()` in `tests/trading/test_scheduler.py` (line 48-53) configures:\\n28\\t```python\\n29\\tmock_query.filter.return_value.first.return_value = None\\n30\\tmock_query.filter.return_value.all.return_value = []\\n31\\t```\\n32\\t\\n33\\tBut does **not** configure `filter.return_value.order_by.return_value.first.return_value`. Because `order_by()` returns an unconfigured `Mock`, calling `.first()` on it returns a truthy `Mock` object instead of `None`.\\n34\\t\\n35\\tThis causes `if position:` in `_process_asset()` to be `True`, leading to `update_candle_tracking()` being called on the mock position, which fails with:\\n36\\t```\\n37\\tTypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for +=: 'Mock' and 'int'\\n38\\t```\\n39\\tat `position.candles_since_entry += 1`.\\n40\\t\\n41\\tThe exception is caught by the bare `except Exception:` handler in `analyze_and_trade()`, incrementing `errors` instead of `processed`.\\n42\\t\\n43\\t---\\n44\\t\\n45\\t## Changes Required\\n46\\t\\n47\\t### Change 1: `quantagent/trading/scheduler.py`\\n48\\t\\n49\\t#### 1a. Add import for `SchedulerHeartbeat`\\n50\\t\\n51\\tAdd `SchedulerHeartbeat` to the existing `from quantagent.models import ...` line (line 16).\\n52\\t\\n53\\t**Before:**\\n54\\t```python\\n55\\tfrom quantagent.models import Environment, Signal, TradeSignal\\n56\\t```\\n57\\t\\n58\\t**After:**\\n59\\t```python\\n60\\tfrom quantagent.models import Environment, SchedulerHeartbeat, Signal, TradeSignal\\n61\\t```\\n62\\t\\n63\\t#### 1b. Add `_upsert_heartbeat_start` method\\n64\\t\\n65\\tAdd after the `_make_thread_id` method (after line 457):\\n66\\t\\n67\\t```python\\n68\\tdef _upsert_heartbeat_start(self, started_at: datetime) -> Optional[\\\"SchedulerHeartbeat\\\"]:\\n69\\t    try:\\n70\\t        existing = (\\n71\\t            self.db.query(SchedulerHeartbeat)\\n72\\t            .filter(SchedulerHeartbeat.environment == self.environment)\\n73\\t            .order_by(SchedulerHeartbeat.id)\\n74\\t            .first()\\n75\\t        )\\n76\\t        if existing is not None:\\n77\\t            existing.timestamp = started_at\\n78\\t            existing.status = \\\"running\\\"\\n79\\t            existing.assets = list(self.config.assets)\\n80\\t            self.db.commit()\\n81\\t            self.db.refresh(existing)\\n82\\t            return existing\\n83\\t\\n84\\t        hb = SchedulerHeartbeat(\\n85\\t            timestamp=started_at,\\n86\\t            status=\\\"running\\\",\\n87\\t            environment=self.environment,\\n88\\t            assets=list(self.config.assets),\\n89\\t        )\\n90\\t        self.db.add(hb)\\n91\\t        self.db.commit()\\n92\\t        self.db.refresh(hb)\\n93\\t        return hb\\n94\\t    except Exception:\\n95\\t        logger.exception(\\\"Heartbeat start failed; continuing cycle\\\")\\n96\\t        return None\\n97\\t```\\n98\\t\\n99\\t**Contract:**\\n100\\t- One row per environment — if a row already exists for `self.environment`, update it in place (upsert).\\n101\\t- Returns `None` on any DB failure; callers must handle this gracefully.\\n102\\t\\n103\\t#### 1c. Add `_upsert_heartbeat_complete` method\\n104\\t\\n105\\tAdd after `_upsert_heartbeat_start`:\\n106\\t\\n107\\t```python\\n108\\tdef _upsert_heartbeat_complete(\\n109\\t    self, heartbeat: Optional[\\\"SchedulerHeartbeat\\\"], stats: Dict[str, float]\\n110\\t) -> None:\\n111\\t    if heartbeat is None:\\n112\\t        return\\n113\\t    try:\\n114\\t        from quantagent.models import Trade\\n115\\t        last_trade = (\\n116\\t            self.db.query(Trade)\\n117\\t            .order_by(Trade.id.desc())\\n118\\t            .first()\\n119\\t        )\\n120\\t        heartbeat.status = \\\"completed\\\"\\n121\\t        heartbeat.completed_at = datetime.utcnow()\\n122\\t        heartbeat.stats = stats\\n123\\t        heartbeat.last_trade_id = last_trade.id if last_trade else None\\n124\\t        self.db.commit()\\n125\\t    except Exception:\\n126\\t        logger.exception(\\\"Heartbeat complete failed\\\")\\n127\\t```\\n128\\t\\n129\\t**Contract:**\\n130\\t- No-op when `heartbeat is None` (graceful degradation when start failed).\\n131\\t- Sets `last_trade_id` to the globally most-recent trade's id (not filtered by environment — consistent with the test expectation in AC-2).\\n132\\t\\n133\\t#### 1d. Modify `analyze_and_trade` to call heartbeat methods\\n134\\t\\n135\\tWrap the existing method body with heartbeat calls:\\n136\\t\\n137\\t**Before (line 148-226):**\\n138\\t```python\\n139\\tdef analyze_and_trade(self) -> Dict[str, float]:\\n140\\t    cycle_start = datetime.utcnow()\\n141\\t    processed = 0\\n142\\t    errors = 0\\n143\\t\\n144\\t    for symbol in self.config.assets:\\n145\\t        ...\\n146\\t\\n147\\t    duration = (datetime.utcnow() - cycle_start).total_seconds()\\n148\\t    stats = { ... }\\n149\\t    self.last_run_stats = stats\\n150\\t\\n151\\t    logger.info(...)\\n152\\t    return stats\\n153\\t```\\n154\\t\\n155\\t**After:**\\n156\\t```python\\n157\\tdef analyze_and_trade(self) -> Dict[str, float]:\\n158\\t    cycle_start = datetime.utcnow()\\n159\\t    processed = 0\\n160\\t    errors = 0\\n161\\t\\n162\\t    heartbeat = self._upsert_heartbeat_start(cycle_start)  # ADD\\n163\\t\\n164\\t    for symbol in self.config.assets:\\n165\\t        ...\\n166\\t\\n167\\t    duration = (datetime.utcnow() - cycle_start).total_seconds()\\n168\\t    stats = { ... }\\n169\\t    self.last_run_stats = stats\\n170\\t\\n171\\t    self._upsert_heartbeat_complete(heartbeat, stats)  # ADD\\n172\\t\\n173\\t    logger.info(...)\\n174\\t    return stats\\n175\\t```\\n176\\t\\n177\\tThe `heartbeat` call is made before the asset loop; `_upsert_heartbeat_complete` is called after `last_run_stats` is set but before the final `logger.info`.\\n178\\t\\n179\\t---\\n180\\t\\n181\\t### Change 2: `tests/trading/test_scheduler.py`\\n182\\t\\n183\\t#### 2a. Fix `DummySession.query()` mock chain\\n184\\t\\n185\\tThe current mock only configures `.filter(...).first()`. It needs to also handle `.filter(...).order_by(...).first()` and `.order_by(...).first()` (used by `_upsert_heartbeat_complete`).\\n186\\t\\n187\\t**Before:**\\n188\\t```python\\n189\\tdef query(self, model):\\n190\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return a mock query object that returns no active positions.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n191\\t    mock_query = Mock()\\n192\\t    mock_query.filter.return_value.first.return_value = None\\n193\\t    mock_query.filter.return_value.all.return_value = []\\n194\\t    return mock_query\\n195\\t```\\n196\\t\\n197\\t**After:**\\n198\\t```python\\n199\\tdef query(self, model):\\n200\\t    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return a mock query object that returns no results.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n201\\t    mock_q = Mock()\\n202\\t    mock_q.filter.return_value = mock_q\\n203\\t    mock_q.order_by.return_value = mock_q\\n204\\t    mock_q.first.return_value = None\\n205\\t    mock_q.all.return_value = []\\n206\\t    return mock_q\\n207\\t```\\n208\\t\\n209\\t**Why this works:** The mock becomes self-referential for all chainable methods (`filter`, `order_by`), so any call sequence ending in `.first()` returns `None` and `.all()` returns `[]`. This covers:\\n210\\t- `query(M).filter(...).order_by(...).first()` → `None` (fixes AC-6, AC-7, AC-8)\\n211\\t- `query(M).filter(...).first()` → `None` (backwards compatible)\\n212\\t- `query(M).order_by(...).first()` → `None` (needed by `_upsert_heartbeat_complete`)\\n213\\t\\n214\\t---\\n215\\t\\n216\\t## Files to Modify\\n217\\t\\n218\\t| File | Change type | Lines affected |\\n219\\t|------|------------|----------------|\\n220\\t| `quantagent/trading/scheduler.py` | Add 2 methods + modify `analyze_and_trade` | ~458–475 (new methods), ~148–227 (modify) |\\n221\\t| `tests/trading/test_scheduler.py` | Fix `DummySession.query()` | lines 48–53 |\\n222\\t\\n223\\t## Files NOT to Touch\\n224\\t\\n225\\t- `quantagent/models.py` — `SchedulerHeartbeat` model is correct as-is\\n226\\t- `quantagent/trading/position_monitor.py` — no changes needed\\n227\\t- `tests/test_vje_scheduler_heartbeat_backend.py` — tests are correct; implementation must match\\n228\\t- `.github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml` — out of scope\\n229\\t\\n230\\t---\\n231\\t\\n232\\t## Verification Commands\\n233\\t\\n234\\t```bash\\n235\\t# Focused gate (8 failing tests)\\n236\\tDATABASE_URL=postgresql://test:test@localhost:5432/quantagent_test \\\\\\n237\\t  /mnt/actions-runner/autodev-runtime/venvs/QuantAgent/.venv/bin/python \\\\\\n238\\t  -m pytest tests/test_vje_scheduler_heartbeat_backend.py tests/trading/test_scheduler.py \\\\\\n239\\t  -v --tb=short --maxfail=10 -m \\\"not integration and not slow\\\"\\n240\\t\\n241\\t# Quick check without PostgreSQL (SQLite fallback)\\n242\\t/mnt/actions-runner/autodev-runtime/venvs/QuantAgent/.venv/bin/python \\\\\\n243\\t  -m pytest tests/test_vje_scheduler_heartbeat_backend.py tests/trading/test_scheduler.py \\\\\\n244\\t  -v --tb=short -m \\\"not integration and not slow\\\"\\n245\\t```\\n246\\t\\n247\\tExpected: all previously-failing tests now show `PASSED`.\\n248\\t\\n249\\t---\\n250\\t\\n251\\t## Risk Assessment\\n252\\t\\n253\\t| Risk | Likelihood | Mitigation |\\n254\\t|------|-----------|------------|\\n255\\t| `_upsert_heartbeat_start` race condition on upsert | Low (single-threaded scheduler) | Acceptable; no unique constraint needed |\\n256\\t| DummySession change breaks currently-passing tests | Low | Self-referential mock is backwards-compatible for all prior patterns |\\n257\\t| `_upsert_heartbeat_complete` importing `Trade` inline causes circular import | Very low | `Trade` is in `models.py`, already imported elsewhere in scheduler |\\n258\\t| Heartbeat writes slow down scheduler cycle | Very low | Commit only 2 extra rows per cycle |\\n259\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"e388d92c-4a3f-4545-9d52-960b86d84a6e\",\"uuid\":\"4ac8df7b-5e29-4828-90e7-c1f55771a9cc\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-09T07:37:40.896Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/azureuser/repos/projects/QuantAgent/docs/06_implementation/QuantAgent-uzq-IM-fix-scheduler-heartbeat.md\",\"content\":\"# QuantAgent-uzq — Implementation: Fix TradingScheduler Heartbeat and Scheduler Unit-Test Regressions\\n\\n**Issue ID:** QuantAgent-uzq  \\n**Phase:** implementer  \\n**Acceptance tests:** `docs/05_acceptance_tests/QuantAgent-uzq-AC-fix-scheduler-heartbeat.md`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Root Cause Analysis\\n\\n### Problem 1 — Missing heartbeat methods in `TradingScheduler`\\n\\nThe `SchedulerHeartbeat` model (`quantagent/models.py:375`) and its tests (`tests/test_vje_scheduler_heartbeat_backend.py`) were written expecting two private methods on `TradingScheduler`:\\n\\n- `_upsert_heartbeat_start(started_at: datetime) -> Optional[SchedulerHeartbeat]`\\n- `_upsert_heartbeat_complete(heartbeat: Optional[SchedulerHeartbeat], stats: dict) -> None`\\n\\nThese methods were never added to `quantagent/trading/scheduler.py`. The `analyze_and_trade()` method (line 148) also never calls them.\\n\\n### Problem 2 — `DummySession.query()` returns an incomplete mock chain\\n\\n`PositionMonitor.get_active_position()` (`quantagent/trading/position_monitor.py:26-36`) chains:\\n```python\\nself.db.query(ActivePosition).filter(...).filter(...).order_by(ActivePosition.id).first()\\n```\\n\\n`DummySession.query()` in `tests/trading/test_scheduler.py` (line 48-53) configures:\\n```python\\nmock_query.filter.return_value.first.return_value = None\\nmock_query.filter.return_value.all.return_value = []\\n```\\n\\nBut does **not** configure `filter.return_value.order_by.return_value.first.return_value`. Because `order_by()` returns an unconfigured `Mock`, calling `.first()` on it returns a truthy `Mock` object instead of `None`.\\n\\nThis causes `if position:` in `_process_asset()` to be `True`, leading to `update_candle_tracking()` being called on the mock position, which fails with:\\n```\\nTypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for +=: 'Mock' and 'int'\\n```\\nat `position.candles_since_entry += 1`.\\n\\nThe exception is caught by the bare `except Exception:` handler in `analyze_and_trade()`, incrementing `errors` instead of `processed`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Changes Required\\n\\n### Change 1: `quantagent/trading/scheduler.py`\\n\\n#### 1a. Add import for `SchedulerHeartbeat`\\n\\nAdd `SchedulerHeartbeat` to the existing `from quantagent.models import ...` line (line 16).\\n\\n**Before:**\\n```python\\nfrom quantagent.models import Environment, Signal, TradeSignal\\n```\\n\\n**After:**\\n```python\\nfrom quantagent.models import Environment, SchedulerHeartbeat, Signal, TradeSignal\\n```\\n\\n#### 1b. Add `_upsert_heartbeat_start` method\\n\\nAdd after the `_make_thread_id` method (after line 457):\\n\\n```python\\ndef _upsert_heartbeat_start(self, started_at: datetime) -> Optional[\\\"SchedulerHeartbeat\\\"]:\\n    try:\\n        existing = (\\n            self.db.query(SchedulerHeartbeat)\\n            .filter(SchedulerHeartbeat.environment == self.environment)\\n            .order_by(SchedulerHeartbeat.id)\\n            .first()\\n        )\\n        if existing is not None:\\n            existing.timestamp = started_at\\n            existing.status = \\\"running\\\"\\n            existing.assets = list(self.config.assets)\\n            self.db.commit()\\n            self.db.refresh(existing)\\n            return existing\\n\\n        hb = SchedulerHeartbeat(\\n            timestamp=started_at,\\n            status=\\\"running\\\",\\n            environment=self.environment,\\n            assets=list(self.config.assets),\\n        )\\n        self.db.add(hb)\\n        self.db.commit()\\n        self.db.refresh(hb)\\n        return hb\\n    except Exception:\\n        logger.exception(\\\"Heartbeat start failed; continuing cycle\\\")\\n        return None\\n```\\n\\n**Contract:**\\n- One row per environment — if a row already exists for `self.environment`, update it in place (upsert).\\n- Returns `None` on any DB failure; callers must handle this gracefully.\\n\\n#### 1c. Add `_upsert_heartbeat_complete` method\\n\\nAdd after `_upsert_heartbeat_start`:\\n\\n```python\\ndef _upsert_heartbeat_complete(\\n    self, heartbeat: Optional[\\\"SchedulerHeartbeat\\\"], stats: Dict[str, float]\\n) -> None:\\n    if heartbeat is None:\\n        return\\n    try:\\n        from quantagent.models import Trade\\n        last_trade = (\\n            self.db.query(Trade)\\n            .order_by(Trade.id.desc())\\n            .first()\\n        )\\n        heartbeat.status = \\\"completed\\\"\\n        heartbeat.completed_at = datetime.utcnow()\\n        heartbeat.stats = stats\\n        heartbeat.last_trade_id = last_trade.id if last_trade else None\\n        self.db.commit()\\n    except Exception:\\n        logger.exception(\\\"Heartbeat complete failed\\\")\\n```\\n\\n**Contract:**\\n- No-op when `heartbeat is None` (graceful degradation when start failed).\\n- Sets `last_trade_id` to the globally most-recent trade's id (not filtered by environment — consistent with the test expectation in AC-2).\\n\\n#### 1d. Modify `analyze_and_trade` to call heartbeat methods\\n\\nWrap the existing method body with heartbeat calls:\\n\\n**Before (line 148-226):**\\n```python\\ndef analyze_and_trade(self) -> Dict[str, float]:\\n    cycle_start = datetime.utcnow()\\n    processed = 0\\n    errors = 0\\n\\n    for symbol in self.config.assets:\\n        ...\\n\\n    duration = (datetime.utcnow() - cycle_start).total_seconds()\\n    stats = { ... }\\n    self.last_run_stats = stats\\n\\n    logger.info(...)\\n    return stats\\n```\\n\\n**After:**\\n```python\\ndef analyze_and_trade(self) -> Dict[str, float]:\\n    cycle_start = datetime.utcnow()\\n    processed = 0\\n    errors = 0\\n\\n    heartbeat = self._upsert_heartbeat_start(cycle_start)  # ADD\\n\\n    for symbol in self.config.assets:\\n        ...\\n\\n    duration = (datetime.utcnow() - cycle_start).total_seconds()\\n    stats = { ... }\\n    self.last_run_stats = stats\\n\\n    self._upsert_heartbeat_complete(heartbeat, stats)  # ADD\\n\\n    logger.info(...)\\n    return stats\\n```\\n\\nThe `heartbeat` call is made before the asset loop; `_upsert_heartbeat_complete` is called after `last_run_stats` is set but before the final `logger.info`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Change 2: `tests/trading/test_scheduler.py`\\n\\n#### 2a. Fix `DummySession.query()` mock chain\\n\\nThe current mock only configures `.filter(...).first()`. It needs to also handle `.filter(...).order_by(...).first()` and `.order_by(...).first()` (used by `_upsert_heartbeat_complete`).\\n\\n**Before:**\\n```python\\ndef query(self, model):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return a mock query object that returns no active positions.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    mock_query = Mock()\\n    mock_query.filter.return_value.first.return_value = None\\n    mock_query.filter.return_value.all.return_value = []\\n    return mock_query\\n```\\n\\n**After:**\\n```python\\ndef query(self, model):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return a mock query object that returns no results.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    mock_q = Mock()\\n    mock_q.filter.return_value = mock_q\\n    mock_q.order_by.return_value = mock_q\\n    mock_q.first.return_value = None\\n    mock_q.all.return_value = []\\n    return mock_q\\n```\\n\\n**Why this works:** The mock becomes self-referential for all chainable methods (`filter`, `order_by`), so any call sequence ending in `.first()` returns `None` and `.all()` returns `[]`. This covers:\\n- `query(M).filter(...).order_by(...).first()` → `None` (fixes AC-6, AC-7, AC-8)\\n- `query(M).filter(...).first()` → `None` (backwards compatible)\\n- `query(M).order_by(...).first()` → `None` (needed by `_upsert_heartbeat_complete`)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Files to Modify\\n\\n| File | Change type | Lines affected |\\n|------|------------|----------------|\\n| `quantagent/trading/scheduler.py` | Add 2 methods + modify `analyze_and_trade` | ~458–475 (new methods), ~148–227 (modify) |\\n| `tests/trading/test_scheduler.py` | Fix `DummySession.query()` | lines 48–53 |\\n\\n## Files NOT to Touch\\n\\n- `quantagent/models.py` — `SchedulerHeartbeat` model is correct as-is\\n- `quantagent/trading/position_monitor.py` — no changes needed\\n- `tests/test_vje_scheduler_heartbeat_backend.py` — tests are correct; implementation must match\\n- `.github/workflows/main-ci-deploy.yml` — out of scope\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Verification Commands\\n\\n```bash\\n# Focused gate (8 failing tests)\\nDATABASE_URL=postgresql://test:test@localhost:5432/quantagent_test \\\\\\n  /mnt/actions-runner/autodev-runtime/venvs/QuantAgent/.venv/bin/python \\\\\\n  -m pytest tests/test_vje_scheduler_heartbeat_backend.py tests/trading/test_scheduler.py \\\\\\n  -v --tb=short --maxfail=10 -m \\\"not integration and not slow\\\"\\n\\n# Quick check without PostgreSQL (SQLite fallback)\\n/mnt/actions-runner/autodev-runtime/venvs/QuantAgent/.venv/bin/python \\\\\\n  -m pytest tests/test_vje_scheduler_heartbeat_backend.py tests/trading/test_scheduler.py \\\\\\n  -v --tb=short -m \\\"not integration and not slow\\\"\\n```\\n\\nExpected: all previously-failing tests now show `PASSED`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Risk Assessment\\n\\n| Risk | Likelihood | Mitigation |\\n|------|-----------|------------|\\n| `_upsert_heartbeat_start` race condition on upsert | Low (single-threaded scheduler) | Acceptable; no unique constraint needed |\\n| DummySession change breaks currently-passing tests | Low | Self-referential mock is backwards-compatible for all prior patterns |\\n| `_upsert_heartbeat_complete` importing `Trade` inline causes circular import | Very low | `Trade` is in `models.py`, already imported elsewhere in scheduler |\\n| Heartbeat writes slow down scheduler cycle | Very low | Commit only 2 extra rows per cycle |\\n\",\"numLines\":259,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":259}}}\ndocs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/executor-stdout-claude-code.log:744:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"input_json_delta\",\"partial_json\":\"velopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/run-report.md\"}},\"session_id\":\"e388d92c-4a3f-4545-9d52-960b86d84a6e\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"1a45ddfe-ad87-4593-bd3d-019940f367ee\"}\ndocs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/executor-stdout-claude-code.log:781:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-6\",\"id\":\"msg_011g79PtNLf1KzSYF1ZBVYbB\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01WJgHDAMdHaC1ZRff7mYNun\",\"name\":\"Write\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/azureuser/repos/projects/QuantAgent/docs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/run-report.md\",\"content\":\"# Run Report — QuantAgent-uzq — implementer\\n\\n**Run-ID:** 20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer  \\n**Phase:** implementer  \\n**Branch:** feature/QuantAgent-uzq-fix-tradingscheduler-heartbeat-and-sched  \\n**Commit:** 833f0a95\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nFixed 8 pre-existing test regressions in TradingScheduler and scheduler unit tests.\\n\\n## Root Causes Addressed\\n\\n### RCA-1 — Missing heartbeat methods (5 tests)\\n`TradingScheduler` had no `_upsert_heartbeat_start` / `_upsert_heartbeat_complete` methods.  \\n`analyze_and_trade()` never called them.\\n\\n**Fix:** Added both methods to `quantagent/trading/scheduler.py` and wired them into `analyze_and_trade()`.\\n\\n### RCA-2 — DummySession mock chain incomplete (3 tests)\\n`DummySession.query()` only configured `.filter().first()` but `PositionMonitor.get_active_position()` calls `.filter().order_by().first()`. The unconfigured `order_by()` returned a truthy Mock, causing `TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for +=: 'Mock' and 'int'` inside `update_candle_tracking()`.\\n\\n**Fix:** Made `DummySession.query()` return a self-referential mock where `filter` and `order_by` both return the same mock object, and `first()` returns `None`.\\n\\n## Files Changed\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `quantagent/trading/scheduler.py` | Add `SchedulerHeartbeat` import; add `_upsert_heartbeat_start`, `_upsert_heartbeat_complete`; wire both into `analyze_and_trade` |\\n| `tests/trading/test_scheduler.py` | Fix `DummySession.query()` self-referential mock chain |\\n\\n## Quality Gates\\n\\n| Gate | Result |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `git status --short` | 2 files changed (scheduler.py, test_scheduler.py) |\\n| `ruff check --fix` (scoped to changed files) | All checks passed |\\n| `python -m compileall -q` (scoped to changed files) | All checks passed |\\n| `pytest tests/test_vje_scheduler_heartbeat_backend.py tests/trading/test_scheduler.py -v -m \\\"not integration and not slow\\\"` | **26 passed, 0 failed** |\\n\\n## Test Results (before → after)\\n\\n| Test | Before | After |\\n|------|--------|-------|\\n| test_upsert_heartbeat_start_updates_existing_row_for_environment | FAIL | PASS |\\n| test_upsert_heartbeat_complete_sets_last_trade_id | FAIL | PASS |\\n| test_analyze_and_trade_continues_when_heartbeat_start_fails | FAIL | PASS |\\n| test_analyze_and_trade_full_cycle_writes_completed_heartbeat | FAIL | PASS |\\n| test_analyze_and_trade_per_asset_error_completes_heartbeat_with_error_count | FAIL | PASS |\\n| test_trading_scheduler_long_signal_executes_order | FAIL | PASS |\\n| test_trading_scheduler_short_signal_executes_order | FAIL | PASS |\\n| test_trading_scheduler_hold_signal_skips_execution | FAIL | PASS |\\n| All other tests in both files | PASS | PASS |\\n\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":159,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":62230,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":159},\"output_tokens\":48,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"e388d92c-4a3f-4545-9d52-960b86d84a6e\",\"uuid\":\"fcfa7f76-f660-40c0-8134-624b65735158\"}\ndocs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/executor-stdout-claude-code.log:784:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01WJgHDAMdHaC1ZRff7mYNun\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"File created successfully at: /home/azureuser/repos/projects/QuantAgent/docs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/run-report.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"e388d92c-4a3f-4545-9d52-960b86d84a6e\",\"uuid\":\"79ad850e-681d-495c-a0b4-ccc6a8f22549\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-09T07:41:10.044Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"create\",\"filePath\":\"/home/azureuser/repos/projects/QuantAgent/docs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/run-report.md\",\"content\":\"# Run Report — QuantAgent-uzq — implementer\\n\\n**Run-ID:** 20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer  \\n**Phase:** implementer  \\n**Branch:** feature/QuantAgent-uzq-fix-tradingscheduler-heartbeat-and-sched  \\n**Commit:** 833f0a95\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nFixed 8 pre-existing test regressions in TradingScheduler and scheduler unit tests.\\n\\n## Root Causes Addressed\\n\\n### RCA-1 — Missing heartbeat methods (5 tests)\\n`TradingScheduler` had no `_upsert_heartbeat_start` / `_upsert_heartbeat_complete` methods.  \\n`analyze_and_trade()` never called them.\\n\\n**Fix:** Added both methods to `quantagent/trading/scheduler.py` and wired them into `analyze_and_trade()`.\\n\\n### RCA-2 — DummySession mock chain incomplete (3 tests)\\n`DummySession.query()` only configured `.filter().first()` but `PositionMonitor.get_active_position()` calls `.filter().order_by().first()`. The unconfigured `order_by()` returned a truthy Mock, causing `TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for +=: 'Mock' and 'int'` inside `update_candle_tracking()`.\\n\\n**Fix:** Made `DummySession.query()` return a self-referential mock where `filter` and `order_by` both return the same mock object, and `first()` returns `None`.\\n\\n## Files Changed\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `quantagent/trading/scheduler.py` | Add `SchedulerHeartbeat` import; add `_upsert_heartbeat_start`, `_upsert_heartbeat_complete`; wire both into `analyze_and_trade` |\\n| `tests/trading/test_scheduler.py` | Fix `DummySession.query()` self-referential mock chain |\\n\\n## Quality Gates\\n\\n| Gate | Result |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `git status --short` | 2 files changed (scheduler.py, test_scheduler.py) |\\n| `ruff check --fix` (scoped to changed files) | All checks passed |\\n| `python -m compileall -q` (scoped to changed files) | All checks passed |\\n| `pytest tests/test_vje_scheduler_heartbeat_backend.py tests/trading/test_scheduler.py -v -m \\\"not integration and not slow\\\"` | **26 passed, 0 failed** |\\n\\n## Test Results (before → after)\\n\\n| Test | Before | After |\\n|------|--------|-------|\\n| test_upsert_heartbeat_start_updates_existing_row_for_environment | FAIL | PASS |\\n| test_upsert_heartbeat_complete_sets_last_trade_id | FAIL | PASS |\\n| test_analyze_and_trade_continues_when_heartbeat_start_fails | FAIL | PASS |\\n| test_analyze_and_trade_full_cycle_writes_completed_heartbeat | FAIL | PASS |\\n| test_analyze_and_trade_per_asset_error_completes_heartbeat_with_error_count | FAIL | PASS |\\n| test_trading_scheduler_long_signal_executes_order | FAIL | PASS |\\n| test_trading_scheduler_short_signal_executes_order | FAIL | PASS |\\n| test_trading_scheduler_hold_signal_skips_execution | FAIL | PASS |\\n| All other tests in both files | PASS | PASS |\\n\",\"structuredPatch\":[],\"originalFile\":null,\"userModified\":false}}\ndocs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/executor-stdout-claude-code.log:791:{\"type\":\"stream_event\",\"event\":{\"type\":\"content_block_delta\",\"index\":0,\"delta\":{\"type\":\"input_json_delta\",\"partial_json\":\"velopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/result.json\"}},\"session_id\":\"e388d92c-4a3f-4545-9d52-960b86d84a6e\",\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"uuid\":\"a4cf4892-6274-4977-b571-cd7bab5c8ed4\"}\ndocs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/executor-stdout-claude-code.log:804:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-6\",\"id\":\"msg_01NZ2Hd4SS5M9gj7qzr1YAc3\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01SL9EowhENh4rQ5bmr7rPrm\",\"name\":\"Write\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/azureuser/repos/projects/QuantAgent/docs/envelopes/QuantAgent-uzq/20260509T024506Z-QuantAgent-uzq-implementer/result.json\",\"content\":\"{\\n  \\